# Copy to .env.local and fill in. See docs/05-SYNC.md for how to create the client id.
#
# This is NOT a secret. An OAuth client id for a browser app is public by construction —
# it ships inside the JavaScript bundle and anyone can read it. What protects the app is
# the "Authorized JavaScript origins" list in Google Cloud Console: the same client id used
# from an origin that is not on that list is refused. There is no client *secret* here,
# because the GIS token model does not use one.
#
# Leave it unset and the app still builds and runs; the sync panel just reports it is off.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=000000000000-abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz012345.apps.googleusercontent.com
